{"availability":"available","full":"OpenMOSS/MOSS-TTS-Nano","name":"MOSS-TTS-Nano","description":"A 100M-parameter multilingual TTS model for real-time CPU inference, voice cloning, and 48 kHz stereo generation","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":4460,"forks":557,"created":"2026-04-10T16:25:07Z","updated":"2026-09-06T06:19:30Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://openmoss.ai/MOSS-TTS-Nano-Demo/","topics":["audio-tokenizer","chinese","cpu-inference","english","multi-modality","multilingual","onnx","realtime","speech-synthesis","streaming-audio","text-to-speech","tts","voice-clone","voice-cloning"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-TTS-Nano","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:50.003Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:50.003Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:50.003Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T13:03:50.003Z","stars":4460,"forks":557}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["MOSS-TTS-Nano is an open-source multilingual tiny speech generation model from MOSI.AI and the OpenMOSS team. With only 0.1B parameters, it is designed for realtime speech generation, can run directly on CPU without a GPU, and keeps the deployment stack simple enough for local demos, web serving, and lightweight product integration.","Start here: Try the demo · Run locally · ONNX CPU inference · Model weights · Fine-tuning","MOSS-TTS-Nano focuses on the part of TTS deployment that matters most in practice: small footprint, low latency, good enough quality for realtime products, and simple local setup. It uses a pure autoregressive Audio Tokenizer + LLM pipeline and keeps the inference workflow friendly for both terminal users and web-demo users."],"features":["MOSS-TTS: the flagship model for high-fidelity zero-shot voice cloning, long-speech generation, fine-grained control over Pinyin, phonemes, and duration, and multilingual/code-switched synthesis.","MOSS-TTS-Local-Transformer: a smaller model in the family based on MossTTSLocal, designed to keep the MOSS-TTS style of speech generation in a lighter model size.","MOSS-TTSD-v1.0: a spoken dialogue generation model for expressive, multi-speaker, and ultra-long dialogue audio.","MOSS-VoiceGenerator: a voice design model that can generate diverse voices and speaking styles directly from text prompts, without reference speech.","MOSS-SoundEffect: a controllable sound generation model for natural ambience, city scenes, animals, human actions, and short music-like audio fragments."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OpenMOSS/MOSS-TTS-Nano/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f46a17046efc4633e7d044385ebb249ec618c9b46c8ea8991b7bf0595e27aa64","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:50.092Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:50.092Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"MOSS-TTS-Nano is an open-source multilingual tiny speech generation model from MOSI.AI and the OpenMOSS team. With only 0.1B parameters, it is designed for realtime speech generation, can run directly on CPU without a GPU, and keeps the deployment stack simple enough for local demos, web serving, and lightweight product integration.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OpenMOSS/MOSS-TTS-Nano/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"MOSS-TTS-Nano is an open-source multilingual tiny speech generation model from MOSI.AI and the OpenMOSS team. With only 0.1B parameters, it is designed for realtime speech generation, can run directly on CPU without a GPU, and keeps the deployment stack simple enough for local demos, web serving, and lightweight product integration.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OpenMOSS/MOSS-TTS-Nano/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f46a17046efc4633e7d044385ebb249ec618c9b46c8ea8991b7bf0595e27aa64","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OpenMOSS/MOSS-TTS-Nano/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:50.092Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-06T06:19:30Z"